"Q24 calculator, style S4b: S4 with the tokenizer rewritten as a *named* loop (Scheme named let)."
"Load after the prelude and S4:"
"  cat docs/experiments/q24_calc_prelude.smol docs/experiments/q24_calc_s4_expr_lib.smol docs/experiments/q24_calc_s4b_named_loop.smol | target/release/smol"
"(S4's own harness run also prints first.)"

"=== Proposed library ==="
"`recur:` hands the block the state and `again`, a block that runs the next iteration."
"Continue = `again value: newState` (in tail position). Stop = answer any other value."
"No Continue/Break classes: a loop the caller owns needs no protocol; Continue/Break remain for"
"iterators the callee owns (do:, folds), where the caller can only ask the callee to stop."
Object >> recur: aBlock [ ^aBlock value: self value: [:next | next recur: aBlock] ]

"=== Calculator: only the tokenizer differs from S4 ==="
Calc4 subclass: #Calc4b instanceVariableNames: ''.

"Outer loop state: pos -> reversed tokens; inner loop state: pos -> value   (records wanted)."
"The inner (number) loop ends by continuing the outer loop directly: `again value: ...`."
Calc4b >> tokensOf: s [
    ^(0 -> nil) recur: [:st :again | | i toks |
        i := st key.
        toks := st value.
        i >= s size
            ifTrue: [toks reversed]
            ifFalse: [| c | c := s at: i.
                self cond: {
                    [c isSpace] -> [again value: i + 1 -> toks].
                    [c isDigit] -> [(i -> 0) recur: [:num :more |
                        (num key < s size and: [(s at: num key) isDigit])
                            ifTrue: [more value: num key + 1 -> (num value * 10 + (s at: num key) digitValue)]
                            ifFalse: [again value: num key -> (Cons with: num value rest: toks)]]].
                    ['+-*/()' includesSubString: c] -> [again value: i + 1 -> (Cons with: c rest: toks)].
                    [true] -> [CalcError signal: 'unexpected ' , c , ' at ' , i asString] }]]
]

(CalcCheck new run: Calc4b new) await.
